2:[["$","section",null,{"className":"wysiwyg-section py-100 md:py-140","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"container ","children":[["$","h1",null,{"className":"h2 mb-56 text-center","children":["$","$L9",null,{"animateOnScroll":"lines","children":"Terms & Conditions · Delegate Pass & Exhibitor Charter"}]}],["$","$La",null,{"className":"max-w-[90rem] mx-auto","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"reset-last wysiwyg--large wysiwyg","dangerouslySetInnerHTML":{"__html":"<p>Welcome to the official portal of <strong>Purple Fest Vadodara 2027</strong>, scheduled for <strong>14–16 January 2027</strong> in <strong>Vadodara, Gujarat (Sanskari Nagari)</strong>. Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 is jointly convened by <strong>Praangan (Vadodara)</strong> and <strong>We Are Together (Brotherhood, New Delhi)</strong> in collaboration with the <strong>Global Inclusive Education Network (GIEN)</strong>, <strong>Tata Institute of Social Sciences (TISS)</strong>, <strong>Department of Empowerment of Persons with Disabilities (DEPwD, Ministry of Social Justice &amp; Empowerment, Govt. of India)</strong>, and the <strong>Office of the State Commissioner for Persons with Disabilities, Government of Goa</strong>.</p>\n<p>By accessing this portal, registering for a Delegate Pass, booking an Exhibition Stall, or submitting an abstract/performance proposal, you agree to be bound by these Terms &amp; Conditions and our Barrier-Free Dignity Charter.</p>\n\n<h2>1. Mandatory Delegate Registration &amp; Strict No-Free-Visitor Policy (₹2,200)</h2>\n<p>In accordance with the Organising Committee’s crowd-safety, sensory-comfort, and universal accessibility mandate:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Mandatory Registration Fee:</strong> Every adult delegate, accompanying professional, academic participant, corporate representative, and general attendee must hold a valid, pre-registered <strong>Delegate Pass priced at ₹2,200 (Indian Rupees Two Thousand Two Hundred Only)</strong> for the full 3-day festival (14–16 January 2027).</li>\n  <li><strong>No Free Casual Walk-In Visitors:</strong> To prevent overcrowding of wheelchair turning radii (1500 mm minimum under IS 4963), tactile paving corridors, and low-sensory zones, <strong>there is no free casual visitor or walk-in public entry</strong>. Entry to all 6 Experience Zones is strictly controlled via QR/Braille-embossed Delegate Badges.</li>\n  <li><strong>What the ₹2,200 Delegate Pass Covers:</strong> Full 3-day access to all 6 Experience Zones, keynote plenaries, GIEN &amp; TISS Inclusive Education sessions, Purple Kaleidoscope cultural evenings, Para-Sports Arena championships, accessible festival kit (Braille/large-print/digital), and on-site ISL interpretation &amp; electric buggy shuttles.</li>\n  <li><strong>Escort / Personal Assistant Policy:</strong> Registered delegates with high-support benchmark disabilities requiring a dedicated personal care attendant or sign-language interpreter must declare their escort during registration so a linked Companion Credential can be issued under the Accessibility Desk protocol.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>2. Exhibition Stall Booking Rules &amp; 4-Tier Fee Schedule (Tiers A, B, C &amp; D)</h2>\n<p>Organizations booking stalls in <strong>Zone 01 (Assistive Tech, Innovation &amp; Startup Expo)</strong> and the NGO/DPO Marketplace are bound by the following 3-day tariff and operational rules:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Tier A — Standard 3m × 3m Octanorm Stall (₹15,000 for 3 Days):</strong> Includes 9 sq.m octanorm shell scheme, fascia board with Braille/high-contrast signage, 1 accessible counter (760 mm knee clearance), 2 chairs, three 15A power sockets, LED spotlights, and <strong>2 complimentary Exhibitor Badges</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier B — Corner / Prime 6m × 3m Double Pavilion (₹35,000 for 3 Days):</strong> Includes 18 sq.m two-side-open prime corner pavilion for CSR Flagships, Ministries, PSUs, and Assistive Tech OEMs, live demo bay, dual accessible counters, and <strong>4 complimentary Exhibitor Badges</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier C — Assistive Startup &amp; University Lab Pod (₹12,000 for 3 Days):</strong> Dedicated innovation pod for DPIIT-recognized assistive tech startups, university R&amp;D labs, and student engineering teams, including demo table, power, and <strong>2 complimentary Exhibitor Badges</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Tier D — Grassroots NGO, DPO &amp; Disabled Artisan Stall (₹5,500 for 3 Days):</strong> Subsidized 3m × 2m stall exclusively for registered Disabled People’s Organisations (DPOs), special schools, and self-help artisan collectives, including display table and <strong>2 complimentary Exhibitor Badges</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Additional Personnel:</strong> Any stall personnel beyond the complimentary badge quota must register for a standard <strong>₹2,200 Delegate Pass</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Barrier-Free Stall Mandate:</strong> Exhibitors must maintain a minimum 1200 mm clear aisle inside/around their stall, provide audio/tactile descriptions of showcased products, and refrain from using strobe lighting (above 3 flashes/second) or unannounced high-decibel PA systems (&gt;75 dB).</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>3. Compliance with the RPwD Act 2016 Across All 21 Benchmark Disabilities</h2>\n<p>Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 operates in strict statutory alignment with India’s <strong>Rights of Persons with Disabilities (RPwD) Act, 2016</strong> and the <strong>UN Convention on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities (UNCRPD)</strong> across all <strong>21 Benchmark Disabilities</strong>:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li>Blindness</li>\n  <li>Low-vision</li>\n  <li>Leprosy Cured Persons</li>\n  <li>Hearing Impairment (Deaf and Hard of Hearing)</li>\n  <li>Locomotor Disability</li>\n  <li>Dwarfism</li>\n  <li>Intellectual Disability</li>\n  <li>Mental Illness</li>\n  <li>Autism Spectrum Disorder</li>\n  <li>Cerebral Palsy</li>\n  <li>Muscular Dystrophy</li>\n  <li>Chronic Neurological Conditions</li>\n  <li>Specific Learning Disabilities (Dyslexia, Dysgraphia, Dyscalculia)</li>\n  <li>Multiple Sclerosis</li>\n  <li>Speech and Language Disability</li>\n  <li>Thalassemia</li>\n  <li>Hemophilia</li>\n  <li>Sickle Cell Disease</li>\n  <li>Multiple Disabilities including Deafblindness</li>\n  <li>Acid Attack Victims</li>\n  <li>Parkinson’s Disease</li>\n</ol>\n<p>Zero tolerance is enforced against any form of ableism, discriminatory language, obstruction of accessible ramps/washrooms/tactile paths, or denial of reasonable accommodation.</p>\n\n<h2>4. Cancellations, Substitutions &amp; Force Majeure</h2>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Delegate Pass Substitutions:</strong> A registered ₹2,200 Delegate Pass may be transferred to another named delegate from the same organization up to <strong>7 January 2027</strong> by emailing <strong>purplefestvadodara@gmail.com</strong>.</li>\n  <li><strong>Stall Cancellation:</strong> Cancellations received in writing before <strong>15 December 2026</strong> are eligible for a 50% refund net of bank/processing charges; cancellations after 15 December 2026 are non-refundable as octanorm fabrication and tactile/Braille directories are finalized.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h2>5. Photography, Livestreaming &amp; Intellectual Property</h2>\n<p>Keynote plenaries, Purple Kaleidoscope performances, and Para-Sports matches are photographed and livestreamed with real-time Indian Sign Language (ISL) and closed captions for educational and advocacy archives by Praangan, Brotherhood, GIEN, and TISS. Delegates who prefer not to be photographed in close-up may request a distinct lanyard indicator at the Registration Desk.</p>\n\n<h2>6. Governing Law &amp; Secretariat Contact</h2>\n<p>These Terms &amp; Conditions are governed by the laws of India, with exclusive jurisdiction in the courts of <strong>Vadodara, Gujarat</strong>. For all official correspondence, contact the Purple Fest Vadodara 2027 Secretariat at <strong>purplefestvadodara@gmail.com</strong> or <strong>+91 98250 93918</strong>.</p>"}}]}]]}]}]]
